        124.97303009033203,
        494.6287536621094,
        134.325927734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "with ½A\u0003z½B\u0003 being constant.",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        147.820068359375,
        423.5994873046875,
        156.77740478515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Population model and artificial data.",
      "bbox": [
        323.60308837890625,
        159.3822784423828,
        479.4874572753906,
        167.18148803710938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Artificial data for",
      "bbox": [
        488.522705078125,
        159.06448364257812,
        554.1909790039062,
        167.28659057617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the conversion process are generated using an ensemble cell",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        169.72274780273438,
        554.1802368164062,
        177.94485473632812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "population model [51], which belongs to the class of Bayesian",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        180.38101196289062,
        554.1614990234375,
        188.60311889648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "hierarchical models. The ensemble consists of single cells whose",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        191.03927612304688,
        554.2179565429688,
        199.26138305664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "stimulus response is governed by the RRE stated above. The",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        201.69754028320312,
        554.1865844726562,
        209.91964721679688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "parameters differ between cells and are drawn from a probability",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        212.35580444335938,
        554.1506958007812,
        220.57791137695312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "distribution. Ensemble models provide a more detailed description",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        223.01406860351562,
        554.195556640625,
        231.23617553710938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of cell populations and are, in principle, advantageous compared",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        233.61581420898438,
        554.2008666992188,
        241.83792114257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to the ODE-MMs. This description of cell-to-cell variability,",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        244.27407836914062,
        554.14892578125,
        252.49618530273438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "namely parameter variability, is thought to be sufficient to describe",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        254.93234252929688,
        554.1668090820312,
        263.1544494628906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "genetic and epigenetic differences between single cells [51,52].",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        265.5906066894531,
        554.2161254882812,
        273.8127136230469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "However, estimating parameters and parameter distributions of",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        276.24884033203125,
        554.2081298828125,
        284.470947265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ensemble models is computationally very demanding. Already a",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        286.9070739746094,
        554.2215576171875,
        295.1291809082031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "single simulation of an ensemble model takes minutes, which limits",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        297.5653076171875,
        554.1893310546875,
        305.78741455078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "their application. As ODE-MMs can be simulated orders of",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        308.16705322265625,
        554.2091064453125,
        316.38916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "magnitudes faster, it is interesting to analyse whether they suffice",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        318.8252868652344,
        554.1946411132812,
        327.0473937988281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for extracting the key properties of the underlying subpopulations.",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        329.4835205078125,
        554.1444702148438,
        337.70562744140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To address this question, we consider two scenarios: (1) a cell",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        340.1417541503906,
        554.1802978515625,
        348.3638610839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "population consisting of two homogeneous subpopulations which",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        350.79998779296875,
        554.228759765625,
        359.0220947265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "do not overlap after stimulation (Figures 2B–D); (2) a cell",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        361.4582214355469,
        554.1802978515625,
        369.6803283691406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "population consisting of two heterogeneous, highly-overlapping",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        372.116455078125,
        554.1166381835938,
        380.33856201171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "subpopulations (Figures 2E–G). In both scenarios the subpopula-",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        382.7746887207031,
        554.173095703125,
        390.9967956542969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tions differ in their responsiveness k1 to the stimulation u(t). The",
      "bbox": [
        315.09832763671875,
        392.9726867675781,
        554.1920166015625,
        402.9588623046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "remaining parameters, k2 and k3, also vary between individual",
      "bbox": [
        315.09844970703125,
        403.63092041015625,
        554.20361328125,
        413.6171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "cells but have the same probability distributions across the two",
      "bbox": [
        315.098388671875,
        414.69268798828125,
        554.1758422851562,
        422.914794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "subpopulations. The probability distribution of the parameters",
      "bbox": [
        315.098388671875,
        425.3509216308594,
        554.1758422851562,
        433.5730285644531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "k~(k1,k2,k3) in the individual subpopulations and scenarios is",
      "bbox": [
        315.098388671875,
        435.6056823730469,
        554.1798095703125,
        444.7195129394531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "depicted in Figures 2D and G. The initial condition of each cell is",
      "bbox": [
        315.0987243652344,
        446.6675109863281,
        554.178955078125,
        454.8896179199219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the steady state reached for u~0 and total concentration,",
      "bbox": [
        315.0987243652344,
        456.9222717285156,
        554.1716918945312,
        465.5478515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "½A\u0003z½B\u0003, equal to one. At t~0, the cells are stimulated, u(t)~1",
      "bbox": [
        315.0987243652344,
        467.28460693359375,
        554.2333984375,
        476.241943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for tw0, resulting in an increase in the abundance of B.",
      "bbox": [
        315.0976867675781,
        478.1822509765625,
        554.202880859375,
        486.8078308105469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Representative trajectory samples are shown in Figures 2A and",
      "bbox": [
        315.09765625,
        489.24395751953125,
        554.1787109375,
        497.466064453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "D. To obtain the artificial measurement data (Figures 2C and F),",
      "bbox": [
        315.09765625,
        499.9021911621094,
        554.201171875,
        508.1242980957031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the abundance of B is measured for 1,000 cells at t~0, 0:1, 0:2,",
      "bbox": [
        315.09765625,
        510.156982421875,
        554.2018432617188,
        518.7825317382812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0:3, 0:5 and 1:0.",
      "bbox": [
        315.09661865234375,
        520.815185546875,
        376.3552551269531,
        529.4407348632812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hypothesis testing.",
      "bbox": [
        323.60308837890625,
        532.0813598632812,
        402.8274230957031,
        539.880615234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Given the artificial data sets, we first",
      "bbox": [
        411.81719970703125,
        531.7636108398438,
        554.1975708007812,
        539.9856567382812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "asked whether ODE-MMs can detect the presence of two",
      "bbox": [
        315.0986328125,
        542.4218139648438,
        554.1770629882812,
        550.6438598632812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "subpopulations and unravel the differences between them. To",
      "bbox": [
        315.0986328125,
        553.080078125,
        554.1842041015625,
        561.3021240234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "address this, we considered four competing hypotheses:",
      "bbox": [
        315.0986328125,
        563.73828125,
        517.5352783203125,
        571.9603271484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "H1 No subpopulations.",
      "bbox": [
        350.9853515625,
        582.5603637695312,
        436.28448486328125,
        590.7824096679688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "H2 Two subpopulations with significantly different",
      "bbox": [
        350.9853515625,
        595.4296875,
        554.12060546875,
        603.6517333984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "stimulus dependent conversion rates A to B (k1,i for",
      "bbox": [
        350.9853515625,
        605.6279296875,
        554.19287109375,
        615.6139526367188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "subpopulation i).",
      "bbox": [
        350.9851379394531,
        616.2860107421875,
        412.2330627441406,
        624.9115600585938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "H3 Two subpopulations with significantly different",
      "bbox": [
        350.98516845703125,
        629.558837890625,
        554.1204223632812,
        637.7808837890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "stimulus independent (basal) conversion rates A to B",
      "bbox": [
        350.98516845703125,
        639.8135986328125,
        554.191162109375,
        648.4391479492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(k2,i for subpopulation i).",
      "bbox": [
        350.98431396484375,
        650.4718017578125,
        442.45086669921875,
        660.4013061523438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "H4 Two subpopulations with significantly different",
      "bbox": [
        350.98565673828125,
        663.8012084960938,
        554.1209106445312,
        672.0232543945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "conversion rates B to A (k3,i for subpopulation i).",
      "bbox": [
        350.98565673828125,
        674.0559692382812,
        533.21533203125,
        684.042236328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "These four scenarios were described using RRE constrained",
      "bbox": [
        324.0557556152344,
        693.2816772460938,
        554.152587890625,
        701.5037231445312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mixture models. To ensure robustness with respect to the",
      "bbox": [
        315.0984191894531,
        703.9398803710938,
        554.1741943359375,
        712.1619262695312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "distribution assumption, we considered normal distribution and",
      "bbox": [
        315.0984191894531,
        714.59814453125,
        554.1785888671875,
        722.8201904296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "log-normal distributions with the mean parameterized by the RRE",
      "bbox": [
        315.0984191894531,
        725.2564086914062,
        554.1903076171875,
        733.4784545898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ODE Constrained Mixture Modelling",
      "bbox": [
        432.39678955078125,
        30.227815628051758,
        554.2755126953125,
        37.54446029663086
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PLOS Computational Biology | www.ploscompbiol.org",
      "bbox": [
        58.052459716796875,
        754.4822998046875,
        243.4130859375,
        761.7988891601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "5",
      "bbox": [
        304.0926208496094,
        754.4822998046875,
        308.15740966796875,
        761.7988891601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "July 2014 | Volume 10 | Issue 7 | e1003686",
